USOS 3.1.2-usos12 patch 0015 (2026-10-18): csmwrap.ini pci_irq_routing

Windows Me on the ASRock X470 (CSM off, CSMWrap SeaBIOS) installs the USOS
I211 NDIS driver but Device Manager disables the card with Code 29 ("the
BIOS did not assign an IRQ"); the same for every other PCI device with an
interrupt pin. Cause: a UEFI board started without CSM routes nothing in
8259 (PIC) mode - on the X470 the Linux log shows LNKA..LNKH "configured
for IRQ 0" (FCH PCI_INTR index 0..7 = 0) and the Interrupt Line registers
are not PIC IRQs. Windows 9x without ACPI has no IRQ steering miniport for
the AMD FCH router, so it can only use what the BIOS assigned. CSMWrap's
$PIR (pir.c) also lists only buses that have their own _PRT, so devices
behind the Promontory switch (the I211 on bus 4, the Wi-Fi, the NVMe) are
missing from it.

With pci_irq_routing = true in csmwrap.ini (written by the Windows 9x flow
only), CSMWrap does what a legacy BIOS POST does, before ExitBootServices:
- walks every PCI bus from the ACPI root bridges (PNP0A08 / PNP0A03,
  _BBN), following bridges by their secondary bus number and the ACPI child
  with the matching _ADR;
- resolves each function's Interrupt Pin through the PIC-mode _PRT (uACPI
  never calls _PIC, so PICM = 0 and _PRT returns the link packages); buses
  without a _PRT use the PCI-to-PCI bridge swizzle (pin + device) mod 4 up
  to the nearest bus that has one;
- for each link device that is actually used: keeps a valid current IRQ
  (_CRS, exactly one IRQ that _PRS allows), otherwise programs one with
  _SRS (the _PRS template reduced to one IRQ; links with dependent functions
  or without _SRS are left alone) and checks it with _CRS. IRQ choice: 11,
  10, 5, 9 allowed by _PRS, least loaded first, busiest links first; 3, 7,
  4, 15, 14, 6, 12 only if _PRS has none of those; never 0, 1, 2, 8, 13;
- writes the IRQ to the Interrupt Line register (0x3C) of every routed
  function and sets those IRQs to level in the ELCR (0x4D0 / 0x4D1);
- pir.c then builds $PIR from this routing: one slot per bus/device with a
  pin, link value 0x80 + link index, bitmap = the one IRQ programmed.
Only PIC-mode routing is touched (on AMD FCH the APIC-mode routing is a
separate register bank); the MADT, the MP table and the ACPI tables are
not changed. Without the ini key the binary behaves as 3.1.2-usos11-int13x.

Own code from the PCI Local Bus 3.0 / PCI-to-PCI Bridge 1.2 specifications,
ACPI 6.5 (6.2.13 _PRT, 6.2.16 _SRS, link devices) and PCI BIOS 2.1 ($PIR).
Applies after 0001-0010, 0012 and 0014, patch -p1 from the top of the
tree. Part of a MODIFIED CSMWrap made by the USOS project (LGPL-2.1).

